`IDocumentIndexer` (`src/storage/kysely/document-indexer.ts`) is the read model behind every relationship question. It indexes exactly two operations — `ADD_RELATIONSHIP` creates an edge, `REMOVE_RELATIONSHIP` removes one — and exposes four queries:

- **`getOutgoing()`** — children and other targets of a document;
- **`getIncoming()`** — parents and other sources;
- **`findPath()`** — path finding by breadth-first search;
- **`findAncestors()`** — the full ancestor graph.

The last two are the ones worth remembering, because they are not derivable from a document's own state at any reasonable cost: a path or an ancestor set spans documents, and each document knows nothing about its parents. The relationship table is indexed on both `sourceId` and `targetId`, which is what makes the graph genuinely bidirectional rather than a parent pointer plus a scan.

`getOutgoing` / `getIncoming` are paged (`{ cursor, limit }`), so enumeration of a large container is DB-native rather than a state read.

